Subject: Index the config scanner's bitmaps with unsigned bytes
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

The scanner's YYCTYPE is char, which is signed on x86-64, so a configuration
byte of 0x80 or above indexed yybm_* below the start of the table. Fil-C
stopped the out-of-bounds read while parsing a configuration with UTF-8 in a
string. Cast the index to unsigned char in the shipped generated scanner
(re2c 4, which Nixpkgs has, is not used to regenerate it).

